    </table>
  </div>

  <p class="note-line">
    Salary figures are self-reported ranges from <a href="https://www.ambitionbox.com/profile/hr-executive-salary" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">AmbitionBox HR executive pay</a> and <a href="https://www.ambitionbox.com/profile/digital-marketing-executive-salary" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">digital marketing executive pay</a>. They are not median outcomes: the low end is common, the top end needs proof and a strong employer.
  </p>

  <div class="highlight-box highlight-box--teal">
    <p>
      <strong>The scalable path inside this lane:</strong> a BA graduate who can write, research and read a dashboard can later offer freelance research, content or reporting services to several clients.
    </p>
    <p>
      That scales because you set your own price, work with more than one client, and can build repeat monthly work instead of one fixed salary.
    </p>
  </div>

  <p class="note-line">
    Want a role-by-role look at humanities pay? See <a href="/blog/career-options/best-paying-jobs-for-humanities-students-india/">best paying jobs for humanities students</a>, or the <a href="/blog/career-options/digital-marketing-career-path-india-role-progression/">digital marketing role progression</a> if that lane appeals.
  </p>

  <h2 id="study-more">Lane 2: study one more degree</h2>

  <p>
    A second degree is worth it when it opens a door your BA cannot, such as teaching, law, or management with a good institute. It is a poor choice when it is a way to avoid deciding.
  </p>

  <div class="study-grid">
