  </div>

  <div class="callout callout--amber">
    <p class="callout__eyebrow">A budget check before any fee</p>
    <ul class="callout__list">
      <li>Take your family's total education and security budget. Treat about 10% for the college as a strict starting benchmark, not a law.</li>
      <li>Spending above roughly 20% needs course-specific proof: placement median, licence requirement, faculty and alumni access.</li>
      <li>Keep the rest for living costs, tools, internet, projects and upskilling after the degree.</li>
    </ul>
    <p class="callout__footer">
      A degree is rarely the whole career system. Money left for skills often decides more than the fee you paid.
    </p>
  </div>

  <p class="note-line">
    Official pages worth checking before you apply: <a href="https://iimcat.ac.in" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">CAT (IIM)</a>, <a href="https://exams.nta.nic.in/cuet-pg/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">CUET PG (NTA)</a>, <a href="https://web.ncte.gov.in/en" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">NCTE</a> and <a href="https://iimc.gov.in" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">IIMC</a>. For the ranked ROI view of courses, read <a href="/blog/college-degrees/best-courses-after-ba-for-good-salary-india/">best courses after BA for good salary</a>.
  </p>

  <h2 id="exam">Lane 3: the exam lane and its real odds</h2>
  <figure class="article-visual"><img src="/images/blog/career-options/ba-career-options/ba-career-options-comparison-lane-exam-lane-real.webp" width="1600" height="1000" loading="lazy" decoding="async" alt="Comparison table of UPSC, SSC CGL, IBPS PO and CTET exam odds, pay or qualification details" title="Lane 3: the exam lane and its real odds" /><figcaption>Exams give the most stable outcome in India and the lowest odds per attempt.</figcaption></figure>

  <p>
    Exams give the most stable outcome in India and the lowest odds per attempt. You can only decide sensibly with the numbers in front of you.
  </p>

  <div class="table-wrap">
    <table class="paths-table">
